ate.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|-20i| \\\\  & =|-20| \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfeet per second." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-318182" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318182" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity of a particle is $(5i-3j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i-3j,\\,a=i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=2\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i-3j)+(i+2j)(2) \\\\  & =(5i-3j)+(2i+4j) \\\\  & =(7i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(10i-6j)\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "(6i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "(6i-j)\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "(7i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}"] ["math" "(7i-j)\\,\\text{m/s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(7i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity of a particle is $(-3i+5j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2i-j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=4\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v=($\n{{field-1}}$i$\n$+$\n{{field-2}}$j\\,)\\,\\text{m/s}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=-3i+5j,\\,a=2i-j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=4\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(-3i+5j)+(2i-j)(4) \\\\  & =(-3i+5j)+(8i-4j) \\\\  & =(5i+1j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-317195" "field" "field-1" "