and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i+j,\\,a=3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=4\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i+j)+(3j)(4) \\\\  & =(5i+j)+(12j) \\\\  & =(5i+13j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(12j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "(17i+j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "(20i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "(5i+13j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "(5i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(5i+13j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity of a particle is $(-i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2},$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=6\\,\\text{h}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=-i+4j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=6\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(-i+4j)+(2i+j)(6) \\\\  & =(-i+4j)+(12i+6j) \\\\  & =(11i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-6i+24j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "(11i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "(11i+6j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "(13i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "(i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136341" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(11i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The initial velocity of a particle is $(5i-j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle after $2$ hours if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(i+3j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i-j,\\,a=i+3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $2$ hours, the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i-j)+(i+3j)(2) \\\\  & =(5i-j)+(2i+6j) \\\\  & =(7i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|7i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{74}\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{74}km/h"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle is $(3i-8j)\\,\\text{km/h},$ and when $t=4\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle is $(15i+8j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle.\n\n$a=($\n{{field-1}}$\\,i$\n$+$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=3i-8j,\\,v=15i+8j,\\,t=4,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 15i+8j & =(3i-8j)+a(4) \\\\ 12i+16j & =4a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{4}(12i+16j) \\\\  & =(3\\,i+4\\,j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-318173" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318173" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318173" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318173" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle is $-8i\\,\\text{km/h},$ and when $t=6\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle is $(4i-18j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle.\n\n$a=($\n{{field-1}}$\\,i$\n$-$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=-8i,\\,v=4i-18j,\\,t=6,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 4i-18j & =-8i+a(6) \\\\ 12i-18j & =6a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{6}(12i-18j) \\\\  & =(2\\,i-3\\,j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-318172" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value"