nd $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=i-6j,\\,v=4i+3j,\\,t=3,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 4i+3j & =(i-6j)+a(3) \\\\ 3i+9j & =3a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{3}(3i+9j) \\\\  & =(i+3j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3i+j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "(2i+3j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "(i+3j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "-3j\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "6i\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(i+3j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle is $(-2i-8j)\\,\\text{m/s},$ and when $t=4\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle is $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=-2i-8j,\\,v=2i,\\,t=4,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 2i & =(-2i-8j)+a(4) \\\\ 4i+8j & =4a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{4}(4i+8j) \\\\  & =(i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136289" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136289" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(i+2j)m/s^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with constant acceleration. The velocity of the particle equals $(-4i+9j)\\,\\text{ft/s}$ both when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$ and $t=7\\,\\text{s}.$ What is the acceleration of the particle?\n\n$a=($\n{{field-1}}$\\,i$\n$+$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=-4i+9j,\\,v=-4i+9j,\\,t=7\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ -4i+9j & =(-4i+9j)+a(7) \\\\ 0 & =7a \\\\ a & =(0\\,i+0\\,j)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-319168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2i+3j)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(-6i-5j)\\,\\text{ft/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(10i+19j)\\,\\text{ft/s}.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{s}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-319168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=-6i-5j,\\,v=10i+19j,\\,a=2i+3j,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 10i+19j & =-6i-5j+(2i+3j)t \\\\ 16i+24j & =(2i+3j)t \\\\ 16i+24j & =2ti+3tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}16=2t \\\\ 24=3t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=8\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-319168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-319168" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-319168" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-2i+j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(6i-8j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(-8i-j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{h}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=6i-8j,\\,v=-8i-j,\\,a=-2i+j,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ -8i-j & =(6i-8j)+(-2i+j)t \\\\ -14i+7j & =(-2i+j)t \\\\ -14i+7j & =-2ti+tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-14=-2t \\\\ 7=t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=7\\,\\text{h}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-318188" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-318188" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-i+7j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(2i-5j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(3i+2j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\na=-i+7j,\\,u=2i-5j,\\,v=3i+2j\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can attempt to solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 3i+2j & =(2i-5j)+(-i+7j)t \\\\ i+7j & =(-i+7j)t \\\\ i+7j & =-ti+7tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1=-t \\\\ 7=7t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answe