+at \\\\ 2i & =(-7i-6j)+(3i+2j)t \\\\ 9i+6j & =(3i+2j)t \\\\ 9i+6j & =3ti+2tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9=3t \\\\ 6=2t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=3\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=1\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=2\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=3\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=6\\,\\text{s}"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=3\\,\\text{s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(i-2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(2i-5j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(3i-j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\na=i-2j,\\,u=2i-5j,\\,v=3i-j\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can attempt to solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 3i-j & =(2i-5j)+(i-2j)t \\\\ i+4j & =(i-2j)t \\\\ i+4j & =ti-2tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1=t \\\\ 4=-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f299e7929890cff147e1e9313cb7800670f9c1cb6cf26837c9cb420b0275ee4"} {"question" "q-136293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=1\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=2\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=3\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "t=4\\,\\text{s}"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "q-136293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d8a3e00c425a9150cc5502fa4cb0da0fd28f7edbc3e3f41bb746db73ea4722"} {"question" "e-9816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $\\mathbf{u}=(5\\mathbf{i} +2\\mathbf{j}) \\,\\textrm{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/example-9816.json" "file_sha256" "b425fc4414c6bcae99e86309e4c93792369e3ca88b7238ba538d38b418ed51ef"} {"question" "e-9816" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|5i+2j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nkilometers per hour." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/example-9816.json" "file_sha256" "b425fc4414c6bcae99e86309e4c93792369e3ca88b7238ba538d38b418ed51ef"} {"question" "e-9818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity of a particle is $(\\mathbf{i} -4\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\textrm{s}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{m/s}^2,$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=5 \\, \\textrm{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/example-9818.json" "file_sha256" "d54f4a1233127611de0d0f68f7ae6b6e85e663b5ec7ec91f9daf80470ce46993"} {"question" "e-9818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} -4\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = 2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j} .\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t = 5 \\, \\textrm{s},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(i-4j)+(2i+j)(5) \\\\  & =(i-4j)+(10i+5j) \\\\  & =(11i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/example-9818.json" "file_sha256" "d54f4a1233127611de0d0f68f7ae6b6e85e663b5ec7ec91f9daf80470ce46993"} {"question" "e-9817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0 \\, \\textrm{h},$ the velocity of the particle is $4\\mathbf{i}  \\, \\textrm{km/h},$ and when $t=3\\, \\textrm{h},$ the velocity of the particle is $(7\\mathbf{i}+15\\mathbf{j})  \\, \\textrm{km/h}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/example-9817.json" "file_sha256" "57314d04b0dd72df610052976b8f5431172445e5bf358207823f5e4842748c91"} {"question" "e-9817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = 4\\mathbf{i}, \\qquad\n\\mathbf{v} = 7\\mathbf{i}+15\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad\nt =3\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $\\mathbf{a}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 7i+15j & =4i+a(3) \\\\ 3i+15j & =3a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{3}(3i+15j) \\\\ a & =(i+5j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/example-9817.json" "file_sha256" "57314d04b0dd72df610052976b8f5431172445e5bf358207823f5e4842748c91"} {"question" "e-9819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{km/h}^2.$ The velocity of the particle is $(-\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\textrm{h}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(3\\mathbf{i}+7\\mathbf{j})  \\, \\textrm{km/h}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/example-9819.json" "file_sha256" "5691b20087de700e59577ef29ab61160c22d43cc52ff49445999ae88974c25c7"} {"question" "e-9819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad\n\\mathbf{u} = -\\mathbf{i} -\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad\n\\mathbf{v} = 3\\mathbf{i}+7\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 3i+7j & =(-i-j)+(i+2j)t \\\\ 4i+8j & =(i+2j)t \\\\ 4i+8j & =ti+2tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4=t \\\\ 8=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/example-9819.json" "file_sha256" "5691b20087de700e59577ef29ab61160c22d43cc52ff49445999ae88974c25c7"} {"question" "q-136288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{74}km/h"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979841/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "b29b96da69b698f58889220f33ac8d95090dddc7013abedd198a20a17786153b" "reviewer_session" "01a108cd-e7f4-73f3-b8fc-c82135bc6b7d" "rationale" "The original question and solution give v=(5i−j)+2(i+3j)=7i+5j, hence speed √(49+25)=√74 km/h, original option c. Saved successful grading agrees. The correction preserves the displayed rate while removing the serialization-only text wrapper." "bindings" {"problem" "4e77c9fb5de607560b794ef1563f383b1f0aa388b0f4ffd12ba546466f837671" "worked_solution" "004261cea9e474ce032de29a6bef983fcf8f0b49cb99a1ebfece7e368e76a71c" "original_field" "7bedb20710b145d2ec557a13ccc9c74fa10703535f7190c995fd491c6eb10016" "reviewed_field" "fba22e3b9e220eeb3d1b4c363e52e2765a9a5c291ab4021b065188150c62cd68" "raw_widget" "4ab9dc3676da214ee7ad6ee4a9759c1f2fc30a8522ec61043c3c8dfa00c0e679"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-136288-before.png" "sha256" "3a3d46ac6f38a9786d958d48255016e528632aae2232696476cf97e57171e7b0"} {"path" "history-q-136288.png" "sha256" "33d1c20581e58532960f343ff22b8fbf932be8535d32ddc63595789965a3bb89"}]} {"question" "q-136288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "8\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "9\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{67}\\,\\text{km/h}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{74}km/h"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Deve